If you haven't taken on the wizard yet, and don't want to know
what it's like, stop reading now!  (Spoilers...)



The wizard seems a lot tougher in 3.1.3 than he used to in 3.0, is
this my imagination or is it real?  Anyway, the problem is this.
After obtaining the bell (from the quest), the candelabrum (from
Vlad, what a wimp!), the barbarian character is pointed in the
direction of the wizard.  The wiz does all his usual tricks - zaps
in lots of monsters, curses lots of gear, creates doubles etc.
Wands of death don't seem to touch him, and it seems to take
AGES before one dies, only to have the other survivor create
another double!  (Infuriating!)

Wielding Magicbane seemed to protect from most of the curses,
and also gave useful probe information every now and then.
What worried me was that the first wizard probed was level
33, the next was level 35, and the next level 38!  Are the
doubles harder than the original, or were the doubles being 
killed first?

It must have taken well over an hour to eventually kill the
wizard and make off with the book of the dead - of course the
wizard kept stealing the other artifacts until they were left
on another level for safety.

Is there a quicker way to do this!  I don't mind it being 
difficult, but it gets a little tedious after a while.
Anyway, I wanted to get on with the next bit, as I hadn't
seen what happened when you had the three artifacts and
you used them on the vibrating square!  (I have now though..)

Does the wizard come after you now into this level?  I haven't
seen him since I left his tower...

Any advice as to what happens in the temple and then on what
is beyond would be gratefully accepted...

